;; K, Under the Stone. The grate in H's floor (columns 17-18) drops onto
;; the rim (row 5); the rough pillars (16, 19) climb back up through it.
;; The cistern's upper half: from the rim's west edge, two glide hops west
;; over the fissure (4-tile gaps, 2 rows down), from the rim's worn lip (15,
;; brittle: take off at a run, never stop on it) to the ledge (9-10) and the
;; lower ledge (3-4), then down the chute (1-2) into L.
;; East, the rim goes on into J, the Bearers' Rest (rows 4-5).
(room
  region: underhum
  at: (7 6)
  title: "Under the Stone"
  intent: "beneath the chamber's floor the great stone's root goes down into an old cistern, and the hum is strongest of anywhere"
  bed: (hum 1.0 air 0.6 water 0)
  light: 0.2
  grid:
  ("################%  %#####"
   "#               %  %    #"
   "#               %  %    #"
   "#               %  %    #"
   "#                        "
   "#                        "
   "#              ##########"
   "#               #########"
   "#        ##     #########"
   "#               #########"
   "#  ##xxxxxxxxxxx#########")
  things: ((root at: (12 1))
           (thin-ice at: (15 6)))
  decor: none)
